NAME
    gcloud alpha design-center spaces application-templates policies delete -
        delete a policy

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha design-center spaces application-templates policies delete
        (POLICY : --application-template=APPLICATION_TEMPLATE
          --location=LOCATION --space=SPACE) [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Delete a policy from an application template.

EXAMPLES
    To delete the policy my-policy for application template my-template in
    space my-space, run:

        $ gcloud alpha design-center spaces application-templates policies \
            delete my-policy --application-template=my-template \
            --space=my-space --project=my-project --location=us-central1

POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
     Policy resource - The policy name in the following format:
     projects/$project/locations/$location/spaces/$space/applicationTemplates/$applicationTemplate/policies/$policy
     The arguments in this group can be used to specify the attributes of this
     resource. (NOTE) Some attributes are not given arguments in this group but
     can be set in other ways.

     To set the project attribute:
      ◆ provide the argument policy on the command line with a fully
        specified name;
      ◆ provide the argument --project on the command line;
      ◆ set the property core/project.

     This must be specified.

       POLICY
          ID of the policy or fully qualified identifier for the policy.

          To set the policy attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument policy on the command line.

          This positional argument must be specified if any of the other
          arguments in this group are specified.

       --application-template=APPLICATION_TEMPLATE
          The applicationTemplate id of the policy resource.

          To set the application-template attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument policy on the command line with a fully
            specified name;
          ▸ provide the argument --application-template on the command line.

       --location=LOCATION
          The location id of the policy resource.

          To set the location attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument policy on the command line with a fully
            specified name;
          ▸ provide the argument --location on the command line.

       --space=SPACE
          The space id of the policy resource.

          To set the space attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument policy on the command line with a fully
            specified name;
          ▸ provide the argument --space on the command line.

